# Azure MCP — Quick Reference (71 tools)

All tools follow the same calling pattern:
```
tool: "<name>"
intent: "what you want"
command: "<sub-command>"      # use learn=true to discover sub-commands
parameters: { ... }
```

## Tier 1 — Daily runbook investigation

| Tool | What it does | When to use |
|------|-------------|-------------|
| `aks` | List/get AKS clusters, node pools, networking | Pods in bad phase, node issues, cluster health |
| `compute` | VMs, VMSS, managed disks — lifecycle & monitoring | Memory/disk/CPU issues on VMs |
| `monitor` | Log Analytics, KQL queries, metrics, activity logs | Query logs, check metrics, inspect activity |
| `resourcehealth` | Resource availability status & service health events | "Is this resource healthy?" |
| `applens` | AI-powered diagnostics — detects root cause & suggests fix | First tool for any "resource is broken" report |
| `containerapps` | List/manage Container Apps | This app's own deployment |
| `datadog` | Datadog monitors via Azure integration | Cross-check Datadog alerts from runbooks |
| `applicationinsights` | List App Insights components | Find APM components (not for querying — use `monitor`) |

## Tier 2 — Infrastructure Context

| Tool | What it does |
|------|-------------|
| `arm` | Azure Resource Graph queries — find/filter any resource |
| `group_list` | List resource groups in a subscription |
| `group_resource_list` | List all resources in a resource group |
